Package: twfeweights
Title: Implicit Weights and Covariate Balance for Difference-in-Differences Estimators
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Brantly", "Callaway", , "brantly.callaway@uga.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes the implicit weights that two-way fixed effects (TWFE)
    regressions and other difference-in-differences estimators place on
    group-time average treatment effects in staggered treatment adoption
    designs. Without covariates, the package recovers the weights that a TWFE
    regression places on each group-time average treatment effect (including
    pre-treatment periods), following de Chaisemartin and D'Haultfoeuille
    (2020) <doi:10.1257/aer.20181169> and Goodman-Bacon (2021)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2021.03.014>, and compares them with the weights
    behind the overall average treatment effect parameters in Callaway and
    Sant'Anna (2021) <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.12.001>. With covariates,
    it writes TWFE regressions and augmented inverse probability weighting
    (AIPW), regression adjustment and inverse probability weighting
    estimators as reweighting estimators and reports how well the implied
    weights balance covariates across treated and comparison groups, as in
    Caetano and Callaway (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2406.15288>.
